# page.zd — a page a content site would actually serve.
#
# Every element here was unreachable before the vocabulary opened: the
# language could emit `div`, `span`, `h2`, `button` and `input`, so a
# portfolio could not render a paragraph, a list, an image, or a link.
#
# Three things this file exists to demonstrate, each of which the parity
# test in `crates/zdc-codegen/tests/page_parity.rs` drives in a real
# JavaScript engine rather than asserting about the source:
#
#   1. The document has landmarks and an outline. `Navigation`, `Main` and
#      `Article` are real `nav`, `main` and `article` elements, and the
#      headings inside them are `h1` and `h2` — chosen by nesting, not
#      written down, so the outline cannot skip a level.
#   2. Links are real anchors with real `href`s, including ones built from
#      data by `each`.
#   3. The head is the program's. `view title is …` is the whole of the
#      metadata syntax, and it costs no reserved word: it reuses the
#      argument list every element already has.

record Note
    slug  is Text
    title is Text

state notes is client List of Note starting [(Note with slug is "/notes/signals", title is "Signals without a dependency array"), (Note with slug is "/notes/placement", title is "Placement is a property of state")]

state open is client Truth starting no

view title is "Field notes", description is "Short pieces about compilers and interfaces", language is "en-GB"
    Main
        Navigation
            List
                Item
                    Link "/"
                        Text "home"
                Item
                    Link "/notes"
                        Text "notes"
                Item
                    Link "https://example.com/feed.xml"
                        Text "feed"

        Article
            # Depth one, so `h1`. Nothing in this file says so.
            Heading "Field notes"

            Paragraph "Short pieces about compilers and the interfaces people build on top of them."

            Figure
                Image source is "/assets/desk.png", alt is "A desk with a terminal open on a compiler error"
                # A caption is centred under what it captions. It is
                # written here rather than baked into the element's base
                # class, because a caption in a left-aligned figure is a
                # real thing to want and a default in `base.css` would be
                # one a program could not undo without an `!important`.
                Caption "The usual view.", textAlign is "center"

            Section
                # Depth two, so `h2`.
                Heading "Recent"

                List
                    each note in notes
                        Item
                            Link note.slug
                                Text note.title

                Paragraph
                    Text "Published "
                    Time "3 August 2026", exact is "2026-08-03"

            Section
                Heading "Colophon"

                Paragraph
                    Text "Built with "
                    Code "zdc"
                    Text ", which is written in Rust."

                Button "about the stack"
                    on click
                        set open to not open

                if open
                    Terms
                        Term "Compiler"
                        Description "Rust, no runtime dependencies"
                        Term "Runtime"
                        Description "Two modules, no framework"

        Footer
            Paragraph
                Emphasis "Everything here is one file."
